h Korea's media landscape, headquartered at the MBC Sangam Headquarters in Seoul. It emerged during a transformative period in South Korean history, marked by rapid industrialization and democratization, and has since played a pivotal role in shaping cultural narratives across East Asia. Under the leadership of influential figures such as Lee Sang-bok, MBC has fostered a rich environment for the production of television dramas, news, and variety programs, contributing significantly to the Korean Wave (Hallyu) that has captivated global audiences.

